G2316.b:
⟪θεός⟫, -οῦ, ὁ, ἡ (⟦Acts 19:37|Ac 19:37⟧ only; v. M, Pr., 60, 244), late voc., θεέ (⟦Matthew 27:46|Mt 27:46⟧; cf. ⟦Deuteronomy 3:24|De 3:24⟧, al.),
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨אֱלֹהִים⁩, also for ⁨אֵל⁩ and other cognate forms, ⁨יהוה⁩, etc.;] ⟪a god or deity⟫, ⟪God⟫.
⟪1.⟫ In polytheistic sense, ⟪a god⟫ or ⟪deity⟫: ⟦Acts 28:6|Ac 28:6⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 8:4|I Co 8:4⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:4|II Th 2:4⟧, al.; pl., ⟦Acts 14:11|Ac. 14:11⟧ ⟦Acts 19:26|19:26⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:8|Ga 4:8⟧, al.
⟪2.⟫ Of the one true ⟪God⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ anarthrous: Mt 6:24, Lk 20:38, al.; esp. c. prep. (Kühner3, iii, 605), ἀπὸ θ., ⟦John 3:2|Jo 3:2⟧; ἐκ, ⟦Acts 5:39|Ac 5:39⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 5:1|II Co 5:1⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:9|Phl 3:9⟧; ὑπό, ⟦Romans 13:1|Ro 13:1⟧; παρὰ θεοῦ, ⟦John 1:6|Jo 1:6⟧; παρὰ θεῷ, ⟦2 Thessalonians 1:6|II Th 1:6⟧, ⟦1 Peter 2:4|I Pe 2:4⟧; κατὰ θεόν, ⟦Romans 8:27|Ro 8:27⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 7:9|II Co 7:9⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 7:10|10⟧; also when in gen. dependent on an anarth. noun (Bl., §46, 6), ⟦Matthew 27:43|Mt 27:43⟧, ⟦Luke 3:2|Lk 3:2⟧, ⟦Romans 1:17|Ro 1:17⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:13|I Th 2:13⟧; as pred., ⟦Luke 20:38|Lk 20:38⟧, ⟦John 1:1|Jo 1:1⟧, and when the nature and character rather than the person of God is meant, ⟦Acts 5:29|Ac 5:29⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:6|Ga 2:6⟧, al. (M, Th., 14);
	⟪(b)⟫ more freq., c. art.: ⟦Matthew 1:23|Mt 1:23⟧, ⟦Mark 2:7|Mk 2:7⟧, al. mult.; c. prep., ἀπὸ τ. θ., ⟦Luke 1:26|Lk 1:26⟧; ἐκ, ⟦John 8:42|Jo 8:42⟧, al.; παρὰ τοῦ θ., ⟦John 8:40|Jo 8:40⟧; π. τῷ θ., ⟦Romans 9:14|Ro 9:14⟧; ἐν, ⟦Colossians 3:3|Col 3:3⟧; ἐπὶ τῷ θ., ⟦Luke 1:47|Lk 1:47⟧; ἐπὶ τὸν θ., ⟦Acts 15:19|Ac 15:19⟧; εἰς τ. θ., ⟦Acts 24:15|Ac 24:15⟧; πρὸς τ. θ., ⟦John 1:2|Jo 1:2⟧; c. gen. pers., ⟦Matthew 22:32|Mt 22:32⟧, ⟦Mark 12:26|Mk 12:26⟧, ⟦Mark 12:26|27⟧, ⟦Luke 20:37|Lk 20:37⟧, ⟦John 20:17|Jo 20:17⟧, al.; ὁ θ. μου, ⟦Romans 1:8|Ro 1:8⟧, ⟦Philippians 1:3|Phl 1:3⟧, al.; ὁ θ. καὶ πατήρ κ. τ. λ., ⟦Romans 15:6|Ro 15:6⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:3|Eph 1:3⟧, ⟦Philippians 4:20|Phl 4:20⟧, al.; c. gen. rei, ⟦Romans 15:5|Ro 15:5⟧, ⟦Romans 15:13|13⟧, ⟦Romans 15:33|33⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 1:3|II Co 1:3⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:23|I Th 5:23⟧; τὰ τ. θεοῦ, ⟦Matthew 16:23|Mt 16:23⟧, ⟦Mark 12:17|Mk 12:17⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:11|I Co 2:11⟧; τὰ πρὸς τὸν θ., ⟦Romans 15:17|Ro 15:17⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:17|He 2:17⟧ ⟦Hebrews 5:1|5:1⟧; τ. θεῷ, as a superl. (LXX, ⟦Joshua 3:3|Jos 3:3⟧), ⟦Acts 7:20|Ac 7:20⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:4|II Co 10:4⟧; Hebraistically, of judges (Ps 81(82):6), ⟦John 10:34|Jo 10:34⟧(LXX), ⟦John 10:35|35⟧.

G2326.b:
⟪θερισμός⟫, -οῦ, ὁ
(< θερίζω), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨קָצִיר⁩;] ⟪harvest⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ the act: ⟦John 4:35|Jo 4:35⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ the time: fig., ⟦Matthew 13:30|Mt 13:30⟧, ⟦Matthew 13:39|39⟧, ⟦Mark 4:29|Mk 4:29⟧
⟪(c)⟫ the crop: fig., ⟦Matthew 9:37|Mt 9:37⟧, ⟦Matthew 9:38|38⟧, ⟦Luke 10:2|Lk 10:2⟧, ⟦Revelation 14:15|Re 14:15⟧.†

G2344.b:
⟪θησαυρός⟫, -οῦ, ὁ
(< τίθημι), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨אוֹצָר⁩;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪a place of safe keeping⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a casket⟫: ⟦Matthew 2:11|Mt 2:11⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪a treasury⟫ (I Mac 3:29 and freq. in cl.);
	⟪(c)⟫ ⟪a storehouse⟫ (⟦Nehemiah 13:12|Ne 13:12⟧, ⟦Deuteronomy 28:12|De 28:12⟧, al.): ⟦Matthew 13:52|Mt 13:52⟧; metaph., of the soul, ⟦Matthew 12:35|Mt 12:35⟧; τ. καρδίας, ⟦Luke 6:45|Lk 6:45⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪a treasure⟫: ⟦Matthew 6:19|Mt 6:19-21⟧ ⟦Matthew 13:44|13:44⟧, ⟦Luke 12:33|Lk 12:33⟧, ⟦Luke 12:34|34⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:26|He 11:26⟧;θ. ἐν οὐρανῷ (v. Dalman, Words, 206 ff.), ⟦Matthew 19:21|Mt 19:21⟧, ⟦Mark 10:21|Mk 10:21⟧, ⟦Luke 18:22|Lk 18:22⟧; of the knowledge of God through Christ, ⟦2 Corinthians 4:7|II Co 4:7⟧; τ. σοφίας κ. γνώσεως, ⟦Colossians 2:3|Col 2:3⟧.†

G2359.b:
⟪θρίξ⟫, τριχός, ἡ,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨שֵׂעָר⁩;] ⟪hair⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of the head: ⟦Matthew 3:4|Mt 3:4⟧ ⟦Matthew 5:36|5:36⟧ ⟦Matthew 10:30|10:30⟧, ⟦Luke 7:38|Lk 7:38⟧, ⟦Luke 7:44|44⟧ ⟦Luke 12:7|12:7⟧ ⟦Luke 21:18|21:18⟧, ⟦John 11:2|Jo 11:2⟧ ⟦John 12:3|12:3⟧, ⟦Acts 27:34|Ac 27:34⟧, ⟦1 Peter 3:3|I Pe 3:3⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:14|Re 1:14⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of animals: ⟦Mark 1:6|Mk 1:6⟧, ⟦Revelation 9:8|Re 9:8⟧.†

G2364.b:
⟪θυγάτηρ⟫, -τρός, ἡ
(for use of vocat., cf. M, Pr., 71; WH, App, 158), [in LXX for ⁨בַּת⁩ (⟦Genesis 5:4|Ge 5:4⟧, al.), exc. ⟦Judges 21:14|Jg 21:14⟧ B, ⟦2 Chronicles 21:17|II Ch 21:17⟧ (⁨אִשָּׁה⁩);] ⟪a daughter⟫: ⟦Matthew 9:18|Mt 9:18⟧ ⟦Matthew 10:35|10:35⟧, ⟦Matthew 10:37|37⟧ ⟦Matthew 14:6|14:6⟧ ⟦Matthew 15:22|15:22⟧, ⟦Matthew 15:28|28⟧, ⟦Mark 5:35|Mk 5:35⟧ ⟦Mark 6:22|6:22⟧ ⟦Mark 7:26|7:26⟧, ⟦Mark 7:29|29⟧, ⟦Luke 2:36|Lk 2:36⟧ ⟦Luke 8:42|8:42⟧, ⟦Luke 8:49|49⟧ ⟦Luke 12:53|12:53⟧, ⟦Acts 2:17|Ac 2:17⟧(LXX) ⟦Acts 7:21|7:21⟧ ⟦Acts 21:9|21:9⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:24|He 11:24⟧. In NT, as in OT, not in cl.;
⟪(a)⟫ as a form of friendly address (cf. ⟦Ruth 2:2|Ru 2:2⟧, ⟦Ruth 2:22|22⟧ al.): ⟦Matthew 9:22|Mt 9:22⟧, ⟦Mark 5:34|Mk 5:34⟧, ⟦Luke 8:48|Lk 8:48⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ metaph.: sc. κυρίου, ⟦2 Corinthians 6:18|II Co 6:18⟧ (cf. ⟦Isaiah 43:6|Is 43:6⟧);
⟪(c)⟫ of posterity: θ. Ἀαρών, ⟦Luke 1:5|Lk 1:5⟧; Ἀβραάμ, ⟦Luke 13:16|Lk 13:16⟧ (cf. ⟦Isaiah 16:2|Is 16:2⟧, IV Mac 15:28, al);
⟪(d)⟫ of habitation: θ. Σιών, Ἱερουσαλήμ, ⟦Matthew 21:5|Mt 21:5⟧(LXX), ⟦Luke 23:28|Lk 23:28⟧, ⟦John 12:15|Jo 12:15⟧ (cf. ⟦Isaiah 1:8|Is 1:8⟧, ⟦Zechariah 9:9|Za 9:9⟧, al.).†

G2379.b:
† ⟪θυσιαστήριον⟫, -ου, τό
(< θυσιάζω, to sacrifice), [in LXX (where the word first appears) very freq., nearly always for ⁨מִזְבֵּחַ⁩;] ⟪an altar⟫:
⟪(a)⟫ generally, ⟦James 2:21|Ja 2:21⟧; pl., ⟦Romans 11:3|Ro 11:3⟧(LXX); metaph., ⟦Hebrews 13:10|He 13:10⟧ (v. Westc., in l., and esp. his add. note on the history of the word, 455 ff.);
⟪(b)⟫ of the altar of burnt-offering in the Temple, ⟦Matthew 5:23|Mt 5:23⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:24|24⟧ ⟦Matthew 23:18|23:18-20⟧, ⟦Matthew 23:35|35⟧, ⟦Luke 11:51|Lk 11:51⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:13|I Co 9:13⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 10:18|10:18⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:13|He 7:13⟧, ⟦Revelation 11:1|Re 11:1⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of the altar of incense in the sanctuary (⟦Exodus 30:1|Ex 30:1⟧, al.), ⟦Luke 1:11|Lk 1:11⟧; symbolically in Heaven, ⟦Revelation 6:9|Re 6:9⟧ ⟦Revelation 8:3|8:3⟧, ⟦Revelation 8:5|5⟧ ⟦Revelation 9:13|9:13⟧ ⟦Revelation 14:18|14:18⟧ ⟦Revelation 16:7|16:7⟧ (Cremer, 292).†

G2384.b:
⟪Ἰακώβ⟫, ὁ, indecl. (Heb. ⁨יַעֲקֹב⁩), ⟪Jacob⟫;
⟪1.⟫ The patriarch: ⟦Matthew 1:2|Mt 1:2⟧ ⟦Matthew 8:11|8:11⟧, ⟦John 4:5|Jo 4:5⟧, ⟦John 4:6|6⟧, ⟦Acts 7:8|Ac 7:8⟧, al,; as in Heb. (cf. ⟦Numbers 23:7|Nu 23:7⟧, ⟦Isaiah 41:8|Is 41:8⟧, Si 23:12, al.), of his descendants, ⟦Romans 11:26|Ro 11:26⟧(LXX).
⟪2.⟫ The father-in-law of Mary: ⟦Matthew 1:15|Mt 1:15⟧, ⟦Matthew 1:16|16⟧ (on the form as distinct from that of the next word, v. Deiss., BS, 3161)

G2398.b:
⟪ἴδιος⟫, -α, -ον (in Attic usually -ος, -ον),
[in LXX chiefly for pers. suff., also for ⁨לָהֶם⁩, etc.; (τὰ ἴ.) ⁨בֵּיתוֹ⁩;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪one's own⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ of that which is private and personal (in cl. opp. to κοινός, δημόσιος; cf. infr. 3);
	⟪(b)⟫ of property, friends, home, country, etc. (in cl. opp. to ἀλλότριος; in late writers often, like ἑαυτοῦ, with weakened sense, v. M, Pr., 87 ff.; Deiss., BS, 123 f.): ⟦Luke 6:41|Lk 6:41⟧, ⟦John 1:42|Jo 1:42⟧ ⟦John 5:43|5:43⟧, ⟦Acts 2:6|Ac 2:6⟧ ⟦Acts 20:28|20:28⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:21|I Co 11:21⟧, ⟦Galatians 6:5|Ga 6:5⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:9|II Ti 1:9⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:27|He 7:27⟧, ⟦Jude 1:6|Ju 6⟧, al.; πράσσειν τὰ ἴ., ⟦1 Thessalonians 4:11|I Th 4:11⟧; κατὰ τὰς ἰ. ἐπιθυμίας, ⟦2 Timothy 4:3|II Ti 4:3⟧; οἱ ἴδιοι, ⟦John 1:11|Jo 1:11⟧ (M, Pr., 90 f.; Field, Notes, 84) ⟦John 13:1|13:1⟧, ⟦Acts 4:23|Ac 4:23⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 5:8|I Ti 5:8⟧; τὰ ἴδια, one's ⟪home⟫ (Field, Notes, 84), ⟦Luke 18:28|Lk 18:28⟧, ⟦John 1:11|Jo 1:11⟧ ⟦John 16:32|16:32⟧ ⟦John 19:27|19:27⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪peculiar⟫, ⟪distinct⟫, ⟪appropriate⟫, ⟪proper⟫: τὸ ἴ. σῶμα, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:38|I Co 15:38⟧; ἐν τ. ἰ. τάγματι, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:23|I Co 15:23⟧; εἰς τ. τόπον τ. ἴ., ⟦Acts 1:25|Ac 1:25⟧; = αὐτοῦ (v. Deiss., ut. supr.), ⟦Matthew 22:5|Mt 22:5⟧, ⟦John 1:42|Jo 1:42⟧ (cf. Wi 10:1).
⟪3.⟫ Adverbially (v. supr., 1 (a); and cf. WM, 7392);
	⟪(a)⟫ ἰδίᾳ, ⟪severally⟫, ⟪separately⟫: ⟦1 Corinthians 12:11|I Co 12:11⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ κατ’ ἰδίαν, ⟪apart⟫, ⟪privately⟫, ⟪in private⟫: ⟦Matthew 14:13|Mt 14:13⟧, ⟦Matthew 14:23|23⟧ ⟦Matthew 20:17|20:17⟧, ⟦Mark 4:34|Mk 4:34⟧ ⟦Mark 7:33|7:33⟧, ⟦Luke 10:23|Lk 10:23⟧, ⟦Acts 23:19|Ac 23:19⟧, al.
